"""Manage the configuration of sylk-conference and sylk-session, as sip-settings3 does for the SIP SIMPLE clients.

The accounts and general settings are in the SDK's configuration file,
~/.sylkclient/config (or that of the folder given with -c), read and written with
the SDK's configuration manager, which keeps the file's structure and indentation.
The SIP SIMPLE clients (~/.sipclient) and Blink (~/.blink) keep theirs in the same
format: they are never written here, only their accounts' credentials can be
imported (--account import).

The general settings, the sessions (what a room is joined with) and the cameras
(usable by any session) of sylk-conference are in the same file (see sylkrtc.settings).
"""

